TI  - AI-Driven Coffee Plantation Mapping and Monitoring Using Sentinel-2 Multispectral Time Series
AU  - Le N.T.
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of 2026 8th International Conference on Green Technology and Sustainable Development Gtsd 2026
AB  - Accurate and up-to-date mapping of coffee plantations is critical for sustainable agricultural management in tropical regions, yet remains challenging due to smallholder farming structures, mixed cropping systems, and persistent cloud cover. This study proposes a scalable and application-oriented framework for coffee plantation mapping using multi-temporal Sentinel-2 multispectral imagery. Instead of relying on complex multi-sensor fusion or deep learning models, the approach focuses on systematic temporal feature engineering from vegetation index time series, including NDVI and NDMI, to capture both spectral characteristics and seasonal growth dynamics of coffee crops.An automated pipeline is developed for satellite data preprocessing, cloud masking, temporal compositing, and feature extraction, ensuring consistency across time and space. The derived temporal features, including statistical descriptors and seasonal indicators, are used as inputs to tree-based machine learning models for coffee versus non-coffee classification. Experimental results across representative communes in Kon Tum province demonstrate that temporal vegetation-index features significantly outperform single-date spectral inputs, improving overall accuracy from approximately 86–87% to 92–94% and increasing the F1-score for the coffee class to 90–93%.Further analysis shows that the proposed features provide strong spatial and temporal generalization, maintaining robust performance across different regions and years. Compared with more complex approaches, the framework achieves competitive accuracy while remaining lightweight, interpretable, and compatible with existing geospatial data infrastructures. These characteristics make it suitable for operational deployment in regional agricultural monitoring systems, supporting data-driven decision-making for sustainable coffee production.
